<newsitem itemid="805549" id="root" date="1997-08-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-ST Electronic interim net up 62 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-ST Electronic interim net up 62 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     4.83  vs    2.98</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		   4.00  vs    nil</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    4.60  vs    5.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			     130.31  vs   59.70</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	3.06  vs    1.28</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    11.34  vs    6.46</p>
<p>    Interest expense			nil  vs    0.04</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation    4.42  vs    2.10</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 6.92  vs    4.31</p>
<p>    Associates		   (loss)  0.12  vs    0.01 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax					1.97  vs    1.32</p>
<p>Dividend pay date:  Sept 18, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:   Sept 3, 1997</p>
<p>Note - ST Electronic &amp; Engineering Ltd said the figures for the previous corresponding period were before its acquisition of four subsidiaries -- Agilis Communication Technologies Pte Ltd, CET Technologies Pte Ltd, Singapore Engineering Software Pte Ltd and ST Simulation Systems Pte Ltd in January 1997. The latest half figures for the period after the acquisitions.  </p>
<p>The group said it expected to perform better in the second half of 1997, based on its order book of $520 million and its push into new regional markets.</p>
